86222a39-28e9-4c20-b6db-95fe0bb29aea	fcfd2e31-637b-466b-b533-df70f7f1b3af	Cash Flow Management - linkedin	The wildest cash flow turnaround I've seen in years just happened in Phoenix.\n\nSarah Martinez runs a mid-size electrical contracting company. Three months ago, she was sitting on $180K in outstanding invoices and couldn't figure out why her AR felt like quicksand.\n\nHere's what she discovered: Her invoices were going out 8-12 days after job completion. Then she'd wait another 3-4 weeks before following up on late payments. By then, her invoices had fallen into the dreaded "we'll get to it next month" pile at client offices.\n\nThe fix was embarrassingly simple: She started sending invoices within 24 hours and set up automatic reminders at 15, 30, and 45 days. No awkward phone calls. No begging. Just professional, consistent follow-through.\n\nResult? Her average collection time dropped from 67 days to 31 days. That's an extra $90K sitting in her account instead of someone else's.\n\nThe universal lesson here isn't about technology or complicated systems. It's about treating your cash flow with the same urgency you treat safety on the jobsite.\n\nLate payments don't happen because clients can't pay—they happen because paying you isn't top of mind when their AP team sits down on Fridays.\n\nEvery day you wait to invoice is money sitting on the table. Every week without follow-up is interest you're not earning.\n\nI've been helping contractors streamline this exact process through Brikly, and Sarah's story isn't unique. When you make invoicing and AR tracking automatic instead of manual, the results speak for themselves.\n\nIf you're tired of wondering when payments will hit your account, try our 14-day free trial at brikly.net. Your cash flow will thank you.\n\nWho else has a cash flow win to share? Drop your story below—we all learn from each other's successes.	text	"[]"	"[{\\"platform\\":\\"linkedin\\"}]"	\N	\N	draft	{}	\N	\N	2025-12-06 17:00:51.610548+00	202